@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.768 = private unnamed_addr constant [626 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of Django's `RawSQL` function.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ADjango's `RawSQL` function can be used to execute arbitrary SQL queries,\0Awhich can in turn lead to SQL injection vulnerabilities.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom django.db.models.expressions import RawSQL\0Afrom django.contrib.auth.models import User\0A\0AUser.objects.annotate(val=RawSQL(\22%s\22 % input_param, []))\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Django documentation: SQL injection protection](https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/dev/topics/security/#sql-injection-protection)\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-89](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html)\0A", align 1
