@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.819 = private unnamed_addr constant [849 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for exception handlers that catch duplicate exceptions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIncluding the same exception multiple times in the same handler is redundant,\0Aas the first exception will catch the exception, making the second exception\0Aunreachable. The same applies to exception hierarchies, as a handler for a\0Aparent exception (like `Exception`) will also catch child exceptions (like\0A`ValueError`).\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Atry:\0A    ...\0Aexcept (Exception, ValueError):  # `Exception` includes `ValueError`.\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Atry:\0A    ...\0Aexcept Exception:\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `except` clause](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/compound_stmts.html#except-clause)\0A- [Python documentation: Exception hierarchy](https://docs.python.org/3/library/exceptions.html#exception-hierarchy)\0A", align 1
