@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.875 = private unnamed_addr constant [710 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for imports that use the same names as builtins.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AReusing a builtin for the name of an import increases the difficulty\0Aof reading and maintaining the code, and can cause non-obvious errors,\0Aas readers may mistake the variable for the builtin and vice versa.\0A\0ABuiltins can be marked as exceptions to this rule via the\0A[`lint.flake8-builtins.ignorelist`] configuration option.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom rich import print\0A\0Aprint(\22Some message\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom rich import print as rich_print\0A\0Arich_print(\22Some message\22)\0A```\0A\0Aor:\0A```python\0Aimport rich\0A\0Arich.print(\22Some message\22)\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-builtins.ignorelist`\0A- `target-version`\0A\0A", align 1
