@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.921 = private unnamed_addr constant [622 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for duplicate members in a `typing.Literal[]` slice.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ADuplicate literal members are redundant and should be removed.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afoo: Literal[\22a\22, \22b\22, \22a\22]\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afoo: Literal[\22a\22, \22b\22]\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as safe, unless the type annotation contains comments.\0A\0ANote that while the fix may flatten nested literals into a single top-level literal,\0Athe semantics of the annotation will remain unchanged.\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `typing.Literal`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Literal)\0A", align 1
