@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.927 = private unnamed_addr constant [501 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for duplicate union members.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ADuplicate union members are redundant and should be removed.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afoo: str | str\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afoo: str\0A```\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThis rule's fix is marked as safe unless the union contains comments.\0A\0AFor nested union, the fix will flatten type expressions into a single\0Atop-level union.\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `typing.Union`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Union)\0A", align 1
