@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1028 = private unnamed_addr constant [597 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of undefined names.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAn undefined name is likely to raise `NameError` at runtime.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef double():\0A    return n * 2  # raises `NameError` if `n` is undefined when `double` is called\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef double(n):\0A    return n * 2\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- [`target-version`]: Can be used to configure which symbols Ruff will understand\0A  as being available in the `builtins` namespace.\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Naming and binding](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/executionmodel.html#naming-and-binding)\0A", align 1
