@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1052 = private unnamed_addr constant [736 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for static methods that use `self` or `cls` as their first argument.\0AThis rule also applies to `__new__` methods, which are implicitly static.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[PEP 8] recommends the use of `self` and `cls` as the first arguments for\0Ainstance methods and class methods, respectively. Naming the first argument\0Aof a static method as `self` or `cls` can be misleading, as static methods\0Ado not receive an instance or class reference as their first argument.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aclass Wolf:\0A    @staticmethod\0A    def eat(self):\0A        pass\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aclass Wolf:\0A    @staticmethod\0A    def eat(sheep):\0A        pass\0A```\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#function-and-method-arguments\0A", align 1
