@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1073 = private unnamed_addr constant [934 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for assignments to attributes that are not defined in `__slots__`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWhen using `__slots__`, only the specified attributes are allowed.\0AAttempting to assign to an attribute that is not defined in `__slots__`\0Awill result in an `AttributeError` at runtime.\0A\0A## Known problems\0AThis rule can't detect `__slots__` implementations in superclasses, and\0Aso limits its analysis to classes that inherit from (at most) `object`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aclass Student:\0A    __slots__ = (\22name\22,)\0A\0A    def __init__(self, name, surname):\0A        self.name = name\0A        self.surname = surname  # [assigning-non-slot]\0A        self.setup()\0A\0A    def setup(self):\0A        pass\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aclass Student:\0A    __slots__ = (\22name\22, \22surname\22)\0A\0A    def __init__(self, name, surname):\0A        self.name = name\0A        self.surname = surname\0A        self.setup()\0A\0A    def setup(self):\0A        pass\0A```\0A", align 1
