@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1125 = private unnamed_addr constant [764 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of exceptions that alias `TimeoutError`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`TimeoutError` is the builtin error type used for exceptions when a system\0Afunction timed out at the system level.\0A\0AIn Python 3.10, `socket.timeout` was aliased to `TimeoutError`. In Python\0A3.11, `asyncio.TimeoutError` was aliased to `TimeoutError`.\0A\0AThese aliases remain in place for compatibility with older versions of\0APython, but may be removed in future versions.\0A\0APrefer using `TimeoutError` directly, as it is more idiomatic and future-proof.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Araise asyncio.TimeoutError\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Araise TimeoutError\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `TimeoutError`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/exceptions.html#TimeoutError)\0A", align 1
