@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1232 = private unnamed_addr constant [26 x i8] c"unnecessary-nested-literal", align 1
@anon.a6b6a9a55df1a6fb8afb47e1f078e4b4.1233 = private unnamed_addr constant [1634 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for unnecessary nested `Literal`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APrefer using a single `Literal`, which is equivalent and more concise.\0A\0AParameterization of literals by other literals is supported as an ergonomic\0Afeature as proposed in [PEP 586], to enable patterns such as:\0A```python\0AReadOnlyMode         = Literal[\22r\22, \22r+\22]\0AWriteAndTruncateMode = Literal[\22w\22, \22w+\22, \22wt\22, \22w+t\22]\0AWriteNoTruncateMode  = Literal[\22r+\22, \22r+t\22]\0AAppendMode           = Literal[\22a\22, \22a+\22, \22at\22, \22a+t\22]\0A\0AAllModes = Literal[ReadOnlyMode, WriteAndTruncateMode,\0A                  WriteNoTruncateMode, AppendMode]\0A```\0A\0AAs a consequence, type checkers also support nesting of literals\0Awhich is less readable than a flat `Literal`:\0A```python\0AAllModes = Literal[Literal[\22r\22, \22r+\22], Literal[\22w\22, \22w+\22, \22wt\22, \22w+t\22],\0A                  Literal[\22r+\22, \22r+t\22], Literal[\22a\22, \22a+\22, \22at\22, \22a+t\22]]\0A```\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0AAllModes = Literal[\0A    Literal[\22r\22, \22r+\22],\0A    Literal[\22w\22, \22w+\22, \22wt\22, \22w+t\22],\0A    Literal[\22r+\22, \22r+t\22],\0A    Literal[\22a\22, \22a+\22, \22at\22, \22a+t\22],\0A]\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0AAllModes = Literal[\0A    \22r\22, \22r+\22, \22w\22, \22w+\22, \22wt\22, \22w+t\22, \22r+\22, \22r+t\22, \22a\22, \22a+\22, \22at\22, \22a+t\22\0A]\0A```\0A\0Aor assign the literal to a variable as in the first example.\0A\0A## Fix safety\0AThe fix for this rule is marked as unsafe when the `Literal` slice is split\0Aacross multiple lines and some of the lines have trailing comments.\0A\0A## References\0A- [Typing documentation: Legal parameters for `Literal` at type check time](https://typing.python.org/en/latest/spec/literal.html#legal-parameters-for-literal-at-type-check-time)\0A\0A[PEP 586](https://peps.python.org/pep-0586/)\0A", align 1
